{"title":"Walk and Salmon watching (hopefully)","startsAt":"2026-10-06T18:15:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-06T20:15:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"Salmons are expected to be swimming upstream. An annual upward migration. We will spend some time to watch at a few spots and then continue with our walk and return back to the starting point. If you arrive late, pls follow the Humber River Trail heading north and you can catch up with the group.\n\nDistance: 7 to 9km\n\nDifficulty: Very Easy\n\nTrail: Flat Paved Trail\n\n**Transport**\nRecommend taking TTC or Uber.\n\n**TTC**: Get off Old Mill station and walk to the park.\n\n**Parking**: There is Paid & Free Parking available nearby meeting spot. Pls look up if you are driving.\n\n💬 **Stay Connected:**\n***Join Whatsapp Group - [CLICK HERE](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSflzD3fDrU5sLARAT5yDF3OhEu3Vj-2P7ci8mP5FYX46rt1NQ/viewform)***\n***Follow on Instagram - [CLICK HERE](https://www.instagram.com/tam.club/)***","venue":{"name":"Etienne Brule Park","address":"13 Crosby Ave, Toronto","lat":43.652554,"lng":-79.49188,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/0/f/0/highres_523744336.jpeg"}